$$2x + 3y = 16$$

What is the value of $x + y$ in the solution to the system of equations above?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$5$"},{"key":"C","text":"$7$"},{"key":"D","text":"$45$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'C', NULL, E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(7x - 3y) + (2x + 3y) = 29 + 16$, which gives $9x = 45$, so $x = 5$. Substituting back into the second equation: $2(5) + 3y = 16$, so $3y = 6$ and $y = 2$. Therefore $x + y = 5 + 2 = 7$. The value $3$ results from computing $x - y = 5 - 2$ instead, a sign error in forming the requested expression. The value $5$ is just $x$ alone, reflecting incomplete reasoning that stops before adding $y$. The value $45$ is the intermediate product $9x$ before dividing by $9$, which a student might report if they misread the question as asking for $9x$.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"C":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 55, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);























